  "body": "## What is needed\n\nFacing a block to height is a common shop-floor job. `OpParams::Face` already works on `SrcRef::Stock` with no 3D model (`crates/app/src/operation/material.rs`, `crates/app/src/operation/heights_sel.rs`), but a user must manually create stock, set heights, and add the operation across multiple panels.\n\n## Design\n\n- Add a single quick-op command using `BatchCommand` (`crates/app/src/commands/batch.rs`) that creates or updates the setup stock and creates a normal `OpParams::Face` on `SrcRef::Stock` in one undo step.\n- Accept plain machining inputs:\n  - Stock XY size (or existing setup stock).\n  - Top Z and final Z.\n  - Depth per pass (`stepdown`), radial `stepover`, cut direction (`climb`), tool, feed, and plunge feed.\n- Refuse invalid inputs (final Z at or above top Z, non-positive stepdown or stepover, missing tool) at command construction.\n- Expose a compact UI form in the Stock/Sketch area and a matching MCP tool in `crates/app/src/mcp/`.\n\nClean-room rule: use plain machining terms only. Do not copy vendor labels or dialog flows.\n\n**Safety floor:** sets stock dimensions and Z heights that reach posted G-code (`effort:high`).\n\n**Done means:** facing to size from numbers on an empty project creates stock and a `Face` operation, generates, verifies, posts G-code, undoes in one step, and passes UI and MCP tests.\n\nPart of #3045\n",
